      "summary": "Authorities in France confirmed the first known human infection with the Shamonda virus in a patient who later died. The virus, previously associated with livestock and spread by mosquitoes, was detected in the deceased individual; public health officials say no widespread risk to the general population has been identified so far while investigations continue."
