      "summary": "The president of the Seine-Saint-Denis department has formally referred the Defender of Rights to investigate the conditions in which minors are held at the Bobigny court detention facility, following complaints and legal concern about cramped, cold cells, concrete benches, inadequate sanitation including reports of urine bottles, and criticism from lawyers, activists and a local rally calling the situation unworthy of a rule-of-law state."
